================================================================================
 7. WHAT THE PANEL ALREADY LIKED -- DO NOT REBUILD THESE
================================================================================
  - The core computer vision concept genuinely interested the panel
  - Identity detection/matching was called out as a strong feature
  - Snapshot-based monitoring (vs. continuous video) was accepted as a
    reasonable, well-justified tradeoff
  - The exam system itself was NOT seen as the biggest problem

  Their real concerns are concentrated in: UI polish, benchmarking rigor,
  threshold justification, technical requirements, and CV validation.
  Spend Capstone 2 effort there, not re-litigating things that already
  landed well.

